one simple idea might be to request external modules like:

```nix
# a modular service gets a metadata thing like this
serviceRequests = {
  # match name as used in service equivalent like services.postgresql
  postgresql = {
    # let's say we may make multiple (instance?) requests, and this is one
    default = {
      # match the structure of services.postgresql
      ensureDatabases = {
        # ...
      };
    };
  };
};
```

the idea would be that this in itself would not yet do anything, instead exposing relevant info to the service consumer so that they might load such requested services as desired (same environment, different environment, ...).
